+    In addition to the "maximum usage" threshold above, a "minimum usage"
+    threshold can be configured to alert when usage on a mount drops *below*
+    a configured percentage. This is useful for mounts that are normally
+    busy: a sudden near-zero usage reading is usually a sign that the
+    filesystem failed to mount, so what's being measured is really the empty
+    mountpoint directory on the root filesystem rather than genuine freed up
+    space.
+
+    To configure a minimum threshold (optionally alongside a maximum one for
+    the same mount), use a mapping instead of a plain value:
+
+    .. code-block:: yaml
+
+        beacons:
+          diskusage:
+            - /mnt/nfs:
+                minimum: 5%
+                maximum: 80%
+            - /mnt/backups:
+                minimum: 10%
+
+    The plain scalar form used above (``- /: 63%``) keeps behaving exactly as
+    it always has, and is equivalent to only setting ``maximum``.
+
